# Pre-Commit Archive Check

**Before creating any git commit** (when the user asks you to commit), review whether the **Information Archive** member documentation needs updating for the changes being committed.

## Archive Files

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `src/lib/archiveGuide/pageGuides.ts` | Page-by-page how-to entries (`PAGE_GUIDES`) |
| `src/lib/archiveGuide/welcomeSections.ts` | Welcome sections (rules, tips, DFP, etc.) |
| `src/components/archive/ArchiveWelcome.tsx` | Renders the guide; icons in `PAGE_GUIDE_ICONS` |
| `public/archive-guide.html` | Printable offline guide (**generated** — do not edit by hand) |

After changing archive content, run:

```bash
npm run generate-archive-guide
```

Include generated `public/archive-guide.html` in the commit when archive source files changed.

## When to Update Archive

Update when the commit changes **member-visible** behavior:

- New pages, tabs, or workflows regular members can use
- Changed labels, requirements (e.g. RSI verification), or step-by-step flows
- New integrations between pages (update `relatesTo`)
- Offline/guest vs signed-in capability changes

See `.cursor/rules/archive-documentation.mdc` for entry format, examples, and what **not** to document (officer tools, backend internals).

## When Archive Update Is Not Needed

Skip Archive edits for:

- Bug fixes that restore intended behavior already described in Archive
- Super-admin/officer-only dashboards, DB Actions, analytics, moderation
- Parser scripts, migrations, or game-data pipeline with no UI change
- Copy or styling tweaks that do not change what members can do

## Pre-Commit Checklist

Before `git commit`:

- [ ] Scan the staged diff for user-facing UI or workflow changes
- [ ] If yes: update `pageGuides.ts` / `welcomeSections.ts` / icons as needed
- [ ] Run `npm run generate-archive-guide` when archive sources changed
- [ ] Verify entries describe **what members can do**, not implementation
- [ ] Include archive updates **in the same commit** when possible
